      "Language": "spa",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "Label": "UNLABELLED",
          "content": "Ovarian ectopic pregnancy is only 3% of all ectopic, with an incidence of 1:7,000-40,000. In the last 10 years, it has been a rise in incidence. Most patients have vaginal bleeding, abdominal pain and shock data. Less than 300-400 cases are reported in the literature."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE",
          "content": "We present the case of a woman with ovarian ectopic pregnancy of 12 weeks of gestation, who have not suggestive clinical signs and whose diagnosis was incidental despite having a regular prenatal ultrasound."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Ovarian pregnancy is a rare presentation; diagnosis is difficult and often suggested by clinical data, when clinical data fail, more studies are needed to integrate the diagnosis."
        }
      ]},
